  {
    "id": "2117122909638705423",
    "type": "Post",
    "postUrl": "https://x.com/FearlessWolfess/status/2117122909638705423",
    "text": "A sharp rise in air pollution on Sunday again placed Lahore at the top of the world’s most polluted cities, with its air quality index (AQI) reaching 478. AQI readings stood at 379 at Safari Park, 357 at Multan Road and 337.\n\nLahore reaching an AQI of 478 is an environmental and public-health emergency, not just another seasonal smog headline.\n\nHow long will citizens be expected to breathe toxic air while authorities issue warnings and ask people to stay indoors?\n•Clean air is a basic public-health necessity, not a luxury.  \n•Children, elderly people and those with respiratory conditions are particularly vulnerable.  \n•Wearing masks and keeping windows closed are temporary precautions, not long-term solutions.  \n•The government must address vehicle emissions, industrial pollution, crop-residue burning, construction dust and poor urban planning.  \n•Publish transparent, real-time air-quality data and establish measurable targets with accountability.  \nPeople cannot stop breathing, stop working or keep children indoors indefinitely.\n\nLahore needs an effective clean-air strategy, not another winter of warnings and temporary restrictions.\n\n@MaryamNSharif \n@ClimateChangePK \n\n#LahoreSmog #AirPollution #CleanAirIsARight #PublicHealth #EnvironmentalJustice",
    "createdAt": "Mon Nov 02 05:13:30 +0000 2026",
